# Studio deviations for this benchmark - recommendation <tab> reason. The fix leaves these
# alone, the check still runs and reports "exception" with the reason.
18.6.19.2.1	IPv6 stays on: the studio prefers IPv4 instead (DisabledComponents 0x20, Microsoft's recommendation in "Configure IPv6 in Windows" rather than disabling IPv6). The Prefer IPv4 policy is baked into every Level 2 gold.
18.10.6.2	Never enabled (user decision): Microsoft's own policy text says it should not be enabled unless Microsoft recommends it as a security response, because it can cause severe app compatibility issues.
